{# W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action> native host dispatch. The call site is lowered ahead of
   the template by `forge::native_action::render` and stored on
   `action.native_action_rendered`, so this template only emits it: the same division
   of labour every backend uses, and the reason one lowering serves them all. An
   argument that cannot be evaluated costs the call and raises error.execution, and
   the block goes on, as on every backend (§scxml-5.7.1). No script engine is involved. #}
                // W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action name="{{ action.native_action_name | escape_swift }}">
                {{ action.native_action_rendered }}
